 ## Version log
 
+### 2026-07-31, OSP boat-count incorporation: second boat effort stream, crabbing fraction f, OSP-informs-tau, and two interview filters (branch `OSP-boat-count-incorporation`)
+
+The gear-resolved track gains the same boat-effort features as the pooled track (built as Phase 0 through Phase 3, validated by a 14-run batch across both models), on the branch `OSP-boat-count-incorporation`. Changes the boat estimate materially, so confirm by a production run; full review in `development_notes/osp-validation-review-2026-07-31.md`.
+
+-   **OSP second boat effort stream (Phase 1b, the gear-resolved mirror).** The OSP Westport Boat Launch daily boat total (`WBL_boat_counts.xlsx`, `fetch_osp_boat_counts`) enters `crab_bss_gear_resolved.stan` as a second boat effort observation on the same latent boat effort, scaled by `kappa_OSP`; the gear-resolved OSP mean sums `lambda_E_S` over the gear dimension before scaling. Toggle `use_osp_boat_counts`; FALSE reproduces the pre-Phase-1b boat exactly. Validation Step 2 raised the boat about 10% and tightened boat-effort CV 11.9% to 11.0%; the gear-resolved boat tracks the pooled boat within 1 to 2% at every step.
+-   **Crabbing fraction f (Phase 2 + 2b + 3).** Trailer and OSP counts are all boats, so `crab_fraction.R` multiplies boat effort and catch by f in the boat generated quantities only (decoupled from sampling; CPUE invariant; the boat is exactly linear in f), Beta prior centered on `crab_fraction_set` (0.3), updated by the `boats_crabbing` / `boats_total` classification once the WBL egress pilot lands; the PE is f-adjusted too. Per-stratum via `crab_fraction_strata`. 0.3 is a placeholder, not a measured estimate, and is the largest lever on the boat harvest.
+-   **OSP-informs-tau (`osp_scale_is_tau`, Phase 3), production ON.** Lets the dense OSP series identify `tau_boat` (the OSP mean uses `L` = `tau_boat` instead of the free `kappa_OSP`), closing GR-12. Resolved 2026-07-31: the trailer count is an instantaneous snapshot, so the OSP/trailer turnover (posterior `kappa_OSP` = 3.15, 95% [2.50, 3.91]) is real and the old `tau_boat` ~1.2 was a ~2x under-count; validation Step 6 puts the gear-resolved boat at about 27.5k vs Step 3b's 13.8k. Caveat: assumes the snapshot is timed representatively (not a fixed daily peak).
+-   **Two interview filters (`fetch_crab_data_v2.R`, matching the pooled `fetch_crab_data.R`).** Non-crabbing interviews (any `number_of_gear == 0` row, regardless of trip status) and gear-tampered interviews (`gear_tampered == 1`) are dropped. Net effect on the validated 2024-25 set is about 2 interviews (the rest were already excluded by the existing `crabbers > 0` / `min_fishing_time` filters); `gear_tampered` is all blank today. Note: v2 has no `private_boat` gear-time filter (the pooled reader does), so the explicit `number_of_gear == 0` rule partly harmonizes the two readers.
